<%#
  Lina.

  Her portrait, made by tools/build-icons.js: a disc with the school's
  own blurred background inside it. The white around that disc is cut
  away in the build, where the circle is measured rather than assumed —
  not hidden here with a border-radius, because the file is also what a
  browser saves, shares and prints.

  Two kinds, same picture at the two sizes it is shown at: `launcher`
  for the round button in the corner of the page, `face` for the header
  of the panel it opens. Each has a second file at twice the size, for
  the dense screens that nearly all phones now have.

  width and height are set so nothing jumps while she loads. Only the
  panel's copy is lazy: the one in the corner is what a visitor sees
  before anything is clicked, and it must not arrive late.

  Expects: kind ("launcher" or "face"), w, h, site.
%>
<% const sizes = { launcher: [64, 128], face: [56, 112] }[kind]; %>
<img class="ai-her is-<%= kind %>"
     src="/icons/assistant-face-<%= sizes[0] %>.webp?v=<%= site.assetVersion %>"
     srcset="/icons/assistant-face-<%= sizes[0] %>.webp?v=<%= site.assetVersion %> 1x,
             /icons/assistant-face-<%= sizes[1] %>.webp?v=<%= site.assetVersion %> 2x"
     width="<%= w %>" height="<%= h %>"
     <%- kind === "face" ? 'loading="lazy"' : "" %>
     alt="Lina" decoding="async">
